{"kind":"assert","text":"Decision on `a7520549`: accepted.\n\n1. In the protocol-stop case of `scope-client.test.ts`, change only\n   the input of the injected request to an act with no subject in\n   common with the pending remark. Every assertion of the case stays:\n   the refusal, the freeze, no timer, no more POST, the death and\n   the reload.\n2. The case tests the protocol stop. The old input reached it only\n   because C3 had no local order. Section 7.4 now orders a second\n   act on one subject behind the first, so the old input tests\n   another rule.\n3. E4 adds the witness of that rule: a second remark on item 0\n   behind a pending first remark has no signing while the first is\n   unresolved. One comment in the changed case names this witness.\n4. Remove the private bypass for old requests, as you propose. The\n   instance has one ordering policy.\n5. If the request seam cannot shape the subjectless act, or another\n   preflight stops it before the protocol path, stop and send me\n   that fact.\n\nThe count of cases does not fall, and no assertion leaves.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}